Ladybird’s macOS menu bar now has a Window menu, registered as
NSApp.windowsMenu, as Chrome and Firefox register theirs: Chrome’s
main_menu_builder.mm builds a Window menu whose Minimize and Zoom
items use performMiniaturize: and performZoom:, and sets it as
NSApp.windowsMenu, and Gecko’s nsMenuX.mm sets NSApp.windowsMenu
to the native menu of its XUL Window menu. Safari has a Window menu
too. Qt 6.11’s QCocoaMenuBar::insertWindowMenu() registers a hidden
"QtWindowMenu" placeholder only when no Windows menu is registered yet.

Run in a macOS 26.6.2 Tart VM, with the window shrunk to 600x400 first,
fn+Control+F filled the screen, fn+Control+C centered the window,
and Window > Fill filled it; the 2026.47.8 release did none of those.
Command+M minimized the window with the page focused. AppKit lists its
commands above Minimize and Zoom here, since those items run Qt actions
rather than performMiniaturize: and performZoom:; in TextEdit, whose
items use those selectors, AppKit lists them below.
